      "message": "feat(ui): a turning tool is assembled from linked components in the tool library window\n\nThe Component stack group now shows for a lathe-held tool. Its empty\nstack offers only a lathe holder or a boring bar (the lathe resolver's\nroots), then the inserts that fit the holder's seat. The values row of a\nlathe stack shows the gauge length (0), the insert's inscribed circle as\nthe diameter, the nose radius and the orientation, or the resolver's\nrefusal by name. Apply stack lands one undoable SetToolAssembly. A\nspindle tool's empty stack no longer offers a lathe holder.\n\nPinned by tool_library_turning_stack::{\na_turning_tool_is_assembled_from_linked_lathe_components_in_one_undo_step,\na_lathe_stack_the_resolver_refuses_shows_the_refusal_by_name}.\n\nFixes #3898\nFixes #3648\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
